{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Stormbringer: Storm Chaser and Thunder Grip proc from direct spell damage (#1684, #1800)",
  "contract": "#1684 Storm Chaser (300612) and #1800 Thunder Grip (301219) are SPELL_ATTR0_PASSIVE records whose single effect is SPELL_EFFECT_APPLY_AURA with EffectApplyAuraName 42 (SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL) on EffectTriggerSpell 300915 and 301220. Both carry Spell.dbc ProcFlags 0 and had no spell_proc row, so SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs skipped them ('Skip if no proc flags in DBC') and Aura::GetProcEffectMask returned 0 before any effect was examined ('only auras with spell proc entry can trigger proc'): the passives occupied a spellbook slot and could never produce a single proc. Their triggered halves are already native. 300915 is aura 108 (SPELL_AURA_ADD_PCT_MODIFIER) with EffectMiscValue 10 (SPELLMOD_CASTING_TIME), EffectBasePoints -16 / EffectDieSides 1 -> -15%, StackAmount 2, DurationIndex 1 (SpellDuration.dbc 1 = 10000 ms) and EffectSpellClassMask word 1 = 17 = bit 0 | bit 4, matching Torrential Wrath 503352 (SpellFamilyFlags[1] = 1) and Call Lightning 500040 (SpellFamilyFlags[1] = 16) inside SpellFamilyName 22; the scenario reads it on Torrential Wrath because Call Lightning has CastingTimeIndex 0 and no cast time to shorten, while Torrential Wrath's CastingTimeIndex 19 is 2500 ms in SpellCastTimes.dbc, so one stack gives 2500 * 0.85 = 2125. 301220 is Mechanic 8 with DurationIndex 31 (SpellDuration.dbc 31 = 8000 ms) and two enemy-targeted effects, aura 92 (SPELL_AURA_PREVENTS_FLEEING) and aura 191 (SPELL_AURA_USE_NORMAL_MOVEMENT_SPEED), both with stock handlers. The fix is one spell_proc row each with ProcFlags 65536 (PROC_FLAG_DONE_SPELL_MAGIC_DMG_CLASS_NEG - every Stormbringer damage spell inspected has DmgClass 1), SpellTypeMask 1, SpellPhaseMask 2, HitMask 3 and Chance 0, which makes the engine use each record's own ProcChance (33 and 30). Shock 804020 is the trigger: DmgClass 1, SchoolMask 8, no cooldown. The harness cannot force a sub-100% roll, so the discriminator is the proc count over a long burst with the stated false-failure probability, not a live reading of an 8- or 10-second aura at an unpredictable moment. Both counts read zero on the current binary.",
